note('2490','hi','Umm Atiyyah reports the charity goat and sending part to Aisha, followed by the Prophet’s question and it-has-reached-its-place reply. Retain for-eating as the requested object’s purpose and charity as the property’s actual status in Aisha’s answer. The Umm Atiyyah apposition after the already named Nasibih is identity explanation. Preserve the exact source name and complete dialogue.')
note('2490','ur','The entire Urdu supplies the goat/gift/dialogue report. Retain the eating purpose and charity-property qualifier. The identity aside after nasibah is malformed and lacks its closing parenthesis; only its literal identity label may become context, leaving the following ne-is clause and actual report words intact. Do not repair the delimiter or fill a name from Hindi.')

note('2493','hi','The chain/comparison notice actually affirms a finite prayer variant: send mercy upon all of them. Select that own imperative as a qualified transmitted supplication fragment, with ultimate speaker and referent of them unfilled. The replacement comparison to Al Abi Awfa is apparatus, not an added prayer identity.')
note('2493','ur','The source’s later route supplies the actual finite un-sab-par-rahmat-bhej prayer wording while comparing it with Al Abi Awfa. Preserve the asymmetric quote punctuation and literal words. Its ultimate prayer speaker and group referent are not explicitly named in this field; the route/comparison remains context.')

note('2500','hi','The same-chain frame supplies the actual conditional that if clouds cover you, count its thirty days. Preserve this complete conditional/imperative fragment without adding the missing antecedent month or an unprinted ultimate speaker. The preceding route/pointer and final Abu Usamah comparison are context.')
